{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439736-renown-examples","id":439736,"title":"Renown Examples.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T04:57:13-07:00","id":439736,"title":"Renown Examples.","content":"I've read through the Renown examples (i.e. how to gain Renown) and while I understand that you &quot;set your own bar&quot; now, I run a larger game with several other ST, online, so things have to be a bit more structured. Can you guys help me out in giving me examples as to how a werewolf could <i>actively</i> pursue gaining Renown of certain types, with <i>suggested</i> levels (e.g. &quot;taking a mate is Purity, but probably never worth more than Purity 1&quot;) for the examples (and also maybe the examples in the book).<br /> <br /> Much obliged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:14:10-07:00","id":439784,"title":"","content":"A question back to you on this is simply - why do you feel it needs to be more structured?<br /> Sure, you have a big game going with multiple storytellers and groups, but are you worried someone is going to complain that someone else got a softball Renown point?<br /> The point is that these things are actively personal. The &quot;Taking a Mate&quot; for Purity example could easily be the first dot's worth, but if you've got a Rahu that's been so focused on being a killing machine his whole life that he's become distant from humanity, maybe &quot;The Wolf must cleave to the Human&quot; is the only tennant of the Oath of the Moon he's been leaving out. In that way, bringing his adherence to completion could make that act a fifth dot deed.<br /> So my (admittedly still vague) suggestions are this:<br /> Dot 1: A deed that shows some defference to the Renown concept (taken an even-handed position in a dispute when you have reason not to, helping someone uncover some secret-ish knowledge, doing something rather cool that's worth bragging about)<br /> Dot 3: A deed that, while still grander than you've done, marks that this Renown is a regular way of life for you<br /> Dot 5: A deed that brings one of the last bits of you in alignment with that Renown, as per my above thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:38:00-07:00","id":439808,"title":"","content":"I think if you need a structured definition because you have multiple.GMs, you should do it like the Forsaken do. Each gm pretend you are an Elder wolf for a moment, and pow-wow: when the tribe's Caialith sings their greatness, do you believe these new deeds are worth remembering?<br /> <br /> A lot of it IS presentation. 'Drains-the-Oceans is cunning because he was able to buy a chicken sandwich without anyone looking at him funny' vs. 'Drains-the-Ocean is truly one of the People, and we know this, but he walks among the sheep, accepted and welcomed and truly makes his pack strong by the depth of connection he shares to his sacred prey'. <br /> <br /> Its all rule of cool: no one cares when a level 20 wizard does something a level 2 can do - but if a raging berserker survivalist succeeds in surviving a prolonged encounter in a crowd of humans without Kuruth? There is a story there, and maybe some Glory or Honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:31:35-07:00","id":440422,"title":"","content":"This should be structured enough for you, YMMV: <a href=\"http://oldwiki.mindseyesociety.org/index.php/Renown_Guide\" target=\"_blank\">http://oldwiki.mindseyesociety.org/i...p/Renown_Guide</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:28:07-07:00","id":440660,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've seen that and used it before, Ephsy, thanks. But I was looking for something that doesn't rely so much on the 'did X for Y months', and a lot of the Purity stuff is like that, for example. It's cool. I've got a new perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}